<BaseLayout title={'Services: regulated assets onchain, network integrations, developer tooling | The Aha Company'} description={'What The Aha Company does for financial institutions, for protocols and products expanding to Stellar, XRPL or Canton, and for ecosystems and foundations: offer, approach, relevant tech and a linked case study for each.'}>
<main data-main="1"><section><div class="svc_introcontainer"><a class="art_back" data-back="1" href="/">← Back to home</a><div class="lg_header"><p class="cs_eyebrow">Services</p><h1 class="intro_h1">Three doors, one engineering team.</h1><p class="art_lede">Regulated assets onchain for financial institutions. Integrations for protocols and products expanding to a new network. Developer tooling for the ecosystems themselves. The engineers who build the networks’ tooling do the integrations.</p></div><nav aria-label="Sections" class="svc_jumpnav"><a class="svc_pill" href="#institutions">Financial institutions</a><a class="svc_pill" href="#protocols">Protocols and products</a><a class="svc_pill" href="#ecosystems">Ecosystems and foundations</a></nav></div></section><section class="ab_white" id="institutions"><div class="ab_container"><div class="ab_howgrid"><div class="ab_howhead"><p class="cs_eyebrow">For financial institutions</p><h2 class="ab_h2">Regulated assets onchain</h2><p class="art_lede">Stablecoins, tokenized funds and deposits, payment and settlement rails, with the compliance controls in the contract and the operating model your risk committee signs off on.</p></div><a class="svc_casecard w-inline-block" href="/case-studies/societe-generale-forge"><span class="cs_cardlabel-green">Financial institution · Stellar</span><span class="nf_cardtitle">Société Générale-FORGE: EURCV, a regulated euro stablecoin on Stellar mainnet</span><span class="svc_casecta">See case study →</span></a></div><div class="svc_cardgrid"><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">The offer</h3><ul class="svc_list" data-svc="arrows" data-rv="svc-institutions-offer" role="list"><li class="svc_li">Stablecoin issuance and governance: role separation, freeze and clawback, allow and deny lists</li><li class="svc_li">Tokenized funds and deposits, mapped to the legal structure</li><li class="svc_li">Payment and settlement rails, with mint and burn bridges to core banking</li><li class="svc_li">Custody and keys: custodian and MPC integrations, KYT through the custodian</li></ul></div><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">How it runs</h3><ul class="svc_list" data-svc="steps" data-rv="svc-institutions-steps" role="list"><li class="svc_li">Scoping: one technical session on authorities, custody and compliance controls</li><li class="svc_li">Structure: NDA, then an MOU with milestones your team can verify</li><li class="svc_li">Build: a first release on testnet with your operations team, milestone by milestone</li><li class="svc_li">Mainnet and after: deployment, runbooks and handover; we stay on the account</li></ul></div><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">Relevant tech</h3><ul class="cs_pills" data-rv="svc-institutions-tech" role="list"><li class="cs_pill">Soroban</li><li class="cs_pill">Stellar Asset Contract</li><li class="cs_pill">SEP-41</li><li class="cs_pill">XRPL MPT</li><li class="cs_pill">Freeze and clawback</li><li class="cs_pill">Custody and MPC</li><li class="cs_pill">KYT</li><li class="cs_pill">Core banking integration</li></ul></div></div><div class="nf_actions"><a class="btn-primary" href="/contact">Schedule a call</a><a class="btn-secondary" href="/work">See our work</a></div></div></section><section class="footer_section" id="protocols"><div class="ab_container"><div class="ab_howgrid"><div class="ab_howhead"><p class="cs_eyebrow">For protocols and products</p><h2 class="ab_h2">Integration onto a new network</h2><p class="art_lede">Your live protocol or product on Stellar, XRPL or Canton: native contracts, adapters and SDKs, routing and liquidity, matched to the guarantees you already give users.</p></div><a class="svc_casecard w-inline-block" href="/case-studies/lifi"><span class="cs_cardlabel-green">Protocol · Stellar</span><span class="nf_cardtitle">LI.FI: Soroban contracts behind the Stellar integration</span><span class="svc_casecta">See case study →</span></a></div><div class="svc_cardgrid"><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">The offer</h3><ul class="svc_list" data-svc="arrows" data-rv="svc-protocols-offer" role="list"><li class="svc_li">Integration roadmap: your integration surface mapped to the target network</li><li class="svc_li">Native contracts, written for the network rather than ported</li><li class="svc_li">Adapters and SDKs: a typed client for your existing stack</li><li class="svc_li">Routing and liquidity: bridges, exchanges and liquidity plans</li></ul></div><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">How it runs</h3><ul class="svc_list" data-svc="steps" data-rv="svc-protocols-steps" role="list"><li class="svc_li">Roadmap: map the integration surface and size the work</li><li class="svc_li">Proposal: milestone-based scope, with or without an ecosystem program</li><li class="svc_li">Build: contracts, adapters and SDKs tested against your suite</li><li class="svc_li">Mainnet: launch, docs and a maintenance plan your engineers can run</li></ul></div><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">Relevant tech</h3><ul class="cs_pills" data-rv="svc-protocols-tech" role="list"><li class="cs_pill">Soroban</li><li class="cs_pill">Rust</li><li class="cs_pill">TypeScript</li><li class="cs_pill">Stellar Asset Contract</li><li class="cs_pill">Circle CCTP</li><li class="cs_pill">Cross-chain routing</li><li class="cs_pill">Wallet kits</li><li class="cs_pill">Third-party audits</li></ul></div></div><div class="nf_actions"><a class="btn-primary" href="/contact">Schedule a call</a><a class="btn-secondary" href="/work">See our work</a></div></div></section><section class="ab_white" id="ecosystems"><div class="ab_container"><div class="ab_howgrid"><div class="ab_howhead"><p class="cs_eyebrow">For ecosystems and foundations</p><h2 class="ab_h2">Developer tooling and DevX</h2><p class="art_lede">The tooling an ecosystem runs on, built and maintained as public goods, and the programs that take teams from prototype to mainnet.</p></div><a class="svc_casecard w-inline-block" href="/case-studies/stellar-development-foundation"><span class="cs_cardlabel-green">Ecosystem · Stellar</span><span class="nf_cardtitle">Stellar Development Foundation: Scaffold Stellar, Stellar CLI plugin system, Stellar Registry, Nido</span><span class="svc_casecta">See case study →</span></a></div><div class="svc_cardgrid"><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">The offer</h3><ul class="svc_list" data-svc="arrows" data-rv="svc-ecosystems-offer" role="list"><li class="svc_li">DevX audit: two engineers, two weeks, on your real onboarding path</li><li class="svc_li">Tooling roadmap agreed with the ecosystem's engineering team</li><li class="svc_li">CLIs, scaffolding, registries, sandboxes and wallets, built as public goods</li><li class="svc_li">Accelerator and hackathon mentoring</li></ul></div><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">How it runs</h3><ul class="svc_list" data-svc="steps" data-rv="svc-ecosystems-steps" role="list"><li class="svc_li">DevX audit: ranked friction points on the onboarding path</li><li class="svc_li">Roadmap: a prioritised tooling plan</li><li class="svc_li">Build: open-source tooling, with docs</li><li class="svc_li">Maintain: a quarterly public-goods proposal and review</li></ul></div><div class="ab_rolecard"><h3 class="svc_cardlabel">Relevant tech</h3><ul class="cs_pills" data-rv="svc-ecosystems-tech" role="list"><li class="cs_pill">Rust</li><li class="cs_pill">TypeScript</li><li class="cs_pill">CLI plugins</li><li class="cs_pill">Code generation</li><li class="cs_pill">Passkeys</li><li class="cs_pill">Open source</li><li class="cs_pill">SBOMs</li><li class="cs_pill">Release automation</li></ul></div></div><div class="nf_actions"><a class="btn-primary" href="/contact">Schedule a call</a><a class="btn-secondary" href="/work">See our work</a></div></div></section></main>
